 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "Algebraically closed coefficient category",
 "statement": "Fix the global finite-field datum [def-weil-finite-field-fiber]\n$(p,a,q,k_0,k)$, a prime $\\ell\\neq p$, and a scheme $Y$. Set\n$\\Ql=\\mathbf Q_\\ell$, the field of $\\ell$-adic numbers [def-weil-l-adic-numbers], choose an algebraic closure $\\Qlb$ of $\\Ql$ [def-weil-algebraic-closure], and use\nthe rationalized category [def-weil-rationalization-karoubi] $D^b_c(Y,E)$ for every finite\ncoefficient field $E/\\Ql$ [def-weil-l-adic-coefficient-extension]. Let $\\mathcal E_\\ell$ be the directed set of finite\nextensions $E/\\Ql$ contained in $\\Qlb$, ordered by inclusion, in which two elements have the compositum as a common upper bound [def-weil-finite-subextension-directed-set]. For $E\\subset L$ in $\\mathcal E_\\ell$, the transition\nfunctor is the scalar-extension functor $K\\mapsto K\\otimes_E L$ of [def-weil-rationalization-karoubi]; it is an exact functor of triangulated categories [def-weil-triangulated-category, lem-weil-scalar-extension-exact-triangulated], and for $E\\subset L\\subset M$ the canonical isomorphisms $(K\\otimes_EL)\\otimes_LM\\cong K\\otimes_EM$ of [lem-weil-scalar-extension-composition] identify the composite of two transition functors with the direct one. Form a triangulated category $\\mathcal\nC_Y$ whose objects are pairs $(E,K)$ with $E\\in\\mathcal E_\\ell$ and $K\\in\nD^b_c(Y,E)$, and whose morphisms between $(E,K)$ and $(E',K')$ are\n\n$$\n \\Hom_{\\mathcal C_Y}((E,K),(E',K'))\n =\\varinjlim_{\\substack{L\\in\\mathcal E_\\ell\\\\L\\supset E,E'}}\n \\Hom_{D^b_c(Y,L)}\n \\bigl(K\\otimes_E L,K'\\otimes_{E'}L\\bigr),\n$$\n\nthe directed colimit of abelian groups [def-weil-directed-colimit-abelian-groups] over the directed set of $L\\in\\mathcal E_\\ell$ containing $E$ and $E'$, whose transition maps for $L\\subset L'$ send $u:K\\otimes_EL\\to K'\\otimes_{E'}L$ to $u\\otimes_LL'$ composed with the identifications of [lem-weil-scalar-extension-composition]. Thus a morphism is represented by a map $u$ over some common finite extension $L$, and two representatives are equal when they agree after extension to a further common finite extension.\nComposition and distinguished triangles are represented over one common\nfinite extension: the composite of $[L,u]:(E,K)\\to(E',K')$ and $[L',v]:(E',K')\\to(E'',K'')$ is the class of $v\\circ u$ formed over a common finite extension $M\\supset L,L'$; the shift is $(E,K)[1]=(E,K[1])$; and a triangle in $\\mathcal C_Y$ is distinguished when it is isomorphic to the image of a distinguished triangle $K\\otimes_EL\\xrightarrow{u}K'\\otimes_{E'}L\\to C\\to(K\\otimes_EL)[1]$ of $D^b_c(Y,L)$ for some $L\\in\\mathcal E_\\ell$, the cone being the object $(L,C)$. This is the finite-stage pair category [def-weil-pbc-finite-stage-pair-category] with the common-stage cones of [def-weil-pbc-common-stage-cones], formed with the finite stages $D^b_c(Y,E)$ and transition functors of [def-weil-rationalization-karoubi]; that these data satisfy the Verdier axioms of a triangulated category is [thm-weil-pbc-verdier-axioms]. Define\n\n$$\n D^b_c(Y,\\Qlb)=\\mathcal C_Y.\n$$\n\nNo Karoubi completion [def-weil-karoubi-envelope] is taken: the notation $\\mathcal C_Y$ denotes the\ncommon-stage category displayed above, in which no idempotent is formally\nadjoined. Every object, morphism, and distinguished triangle has a finite\ncoefficient field of definition, after enlarging that field if necessary.",
