  "summary": "Checked the statement against the master blueprint node (order 1462) and the slopmaster2 note 42_qbarl_triangulated_colimit.tex (def:finext to thm:pair-triangulated, def:karoubi-triples). The mathematical content is unchanged; the statement now names every notion it is built from: $\\mathbf Q_\\ell$, the algebraic closure and finite extensions (reviewed leaves def-weil-l-adic-numbers, def-weil-algebraic-closure, def-weil-l-adic-coefficient-extension), the directed set $\\mathcal E_\\ell$ (new Mathlib leaf def-weil-finite-subextension-directed-set), the finite stages and transition functors (def-weil-rationalization-karoubi) with the exactness and composition compatibilities the directed Hom system and the triangles need (lem-weil-scalar-extension-exact-triangulated, lem-weil-scalar-extension-composition), the directed colimit of abelian groups (new Mathlib leaf def-weil-directed-colimit-abelian-groups), the notion of triangulated category and exact functor (new Mathlib leaf def-weil-triangulated-category), and the Karoubi envelope it says it does not take (def-weil-karoubi-envelope). The common-stage construction (representatives, transport, equality at a common stage, composition, shift, cones, Verdier axioms) is not restated in new nodes: it is the finite-stage pair category of the proper-base-change chapter, def-weil-pbc-finite-stage-pair-category with def-weil-pbc-common-stage-cones and thm-weil-pbc-verdier-axioms, to which the statement now points; those nodes are written for the finite stages $\\Dbc(T,E)$ of def-weil-pbc-rational-category, the proper-base-change counterpart of def-weil-rationalization-karoubi, and def-weil-pbc-qbar-category (order 1311) states the same object $\\Dbc(T,\\Qlb)=\\mathcal P_T$ as this node; the merge of the two chains is reported to the lead. The hidden steps 'composition and distinguished triangles are represented over one common finite extension' are written out. The slopmaster2 version differs: there $\\Dbc(X,\\Qlb)_{2colim}=\\Kar(\\mathrm{Pair})$ is the Karoubi envelope, while master takes no Karoubi completion and proves idempotent completeness separately (lem-weil-qbar-idempotent-complete, which depends on this node and is therefore not cited here)."
 },
